A||N||26||TwisT||Head-rest Fiero speakers...  How do they sound?||||1||
Z||000000||TwisT||02-08-2001||07:56 PM||||I read somewhere that replacing the Fiero's head-rest speakers with good aftermarket one's supply great stereo imagery to the person sitting in the seat.  Can anyone elaborate on this?  It seems to make sense,  almost giving you the effect of wearing headphones.<P>I don't have them in my '88 GT,  but would definately consider for a future stereo upgrade.  I thought it would be nice to hear some input first.<P>Thanks gang.<P>Brett<BR>Yankton,  SD<BR>'88 "ITALFIERO" GT||||reg||1
Z||000001||Neverfinished||02-08-2001||08:01 PM||||I have them in my 84 and they sound awesome. They work better with an aftermarket cd player. I have an amp runnuing alot of power to them and they sound decent for stock speakers. Of course you would have to fade them more to the front but I think they sound better than the speakers in the sail panels.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Neverfinished||02-08-2001||08:02 PM||||I have them in my 84 and they sound awesome. They work better with an aftermarket cd player. I have an amp runnuing alot of power to them and they sound decent for stock speakers. Of course you would have to fade them more to the front but I think they sound better than the speakers in the sail panels.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Neverfinished||02-08-2001||08:02 PM||||I have them in my 84 and they sound awesome. They work better with an aftermarket cd player. I have an amp runnuing alot of power to them and they sound decent for stock speakers. Of course you would have to fade them more to the front but I think they sound better than the speakers in the sail panels.||||reg||1
Z||000004||2xsess||02-08-2001||08:05 PM||||I have had 3 fieros with them and 2 without, I think the imagery is better with them. All I've ever had is the factory speakers with aftermarket head units. Plus it shocks some people when they finally realize that the sound is coming out of the seat  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>AOL IM : Only2xsess<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/2xsess.gif">      <BR> <A HREF="http://kresgeus.homestead.com/FieroPage.html" TARGET=_blank>Visit My Website</A>||||reg||1
Z||000005||TwisT||02-08-2001||08:29 PM||||I'm curious if one would really have to upgrade the seat's speaker's to get the same effect.  I assume they only provide high frequency response...  <P>Hmm....  I wonder what seperates would sound like in the seats...  lol<P>Brett||||reg||1
Z||000006||PearlBlueSoul||02-08-2001||08:53 PM||||Sail panels?  Sorry, never heard that term before.  Whereabous are the Sail panels?  like, I'm guessing somewhere behind the seats?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif">  or....<P>------------------<BR>1987 Toyota MR2 N/A 5 speed<BR>  <A HREF="http://www.atlantamr2s.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.atlantamr2s.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/darionscard" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/darionscard</A>  <BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/darionscard/Thumb.jpg">       <BR><B>Notable mods:</B>  Sus tech springs and sway bars, Toyota strut tower brace, KYB strut inserts, HKS exhaust, NGK plugs/wires, Momo Racer wheels (14x6), Custom intake, Kenwood 12" speaker in front trunk, Jensen amp.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Seanh||02-08-2001||09:00 PM||||Yep, Sail panels are the interior panels to the sides of the seats to the firewall.<P>Myself, I dont like headrest speakers. I prefer sail panel speakers to headrest speakers any day of the week. Its all up to you and how you like your music.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/transsig.gif">    <BR><A HREF="http://www.kdsi.net/~sean" TARGET=_blank>Sean's Fiero Page</A><BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8 Auto (3.4 Conversion in Progress)<BR><I>"It's always in the last place you look." Of course it is. Why would you keep looking after you've found it? Do people do this? Who and where are they?</I>||||reg||1
Z||000008||PearlBlueSoul||02-08-2001||09:04 PM||||koo.  wished we had those.  got 'em above and behind our heads in the pillars on these.  the later model 2s got sail panel speakers. ||||reg||1
Z||000009||fierosound||02-08-2001||09:08 PM||||neverfinished....  WOW must really be impressive  3 posts...   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by fierosound (edited 02-08-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000010||Neverfinished||02-08-2001||09:35 PM||||ya it is pretty important. Just stressing my point  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <BR>I get too impatient some times and just keep clicking submit reply.<BR>anyways, I have been impressed with the quality of the speakers in the seats and they can handle a decent amount of power. Go with the seat speakers!||||reg||1
Z||000011||William||02-09-2001||12:27 AM||||Here's something that you may not have considered. I just upgraded my seat speakers when I did the new leather last weekend. I got quite a surprize when it was all together and I tested it. Even tho I used bass blockers, I now get quite a thump to the back of my head. It's a cross between a steady vibration and a serious banging. I was having a bad headache the day I was testing them and could not take it for more than a minute. It does give the effect of a small sub in the car and it did improve the presence of the sound. I really like them but I'm not to sure yet about my head vibrating that much... :-)<p>[This message has been edited by William (edited 02-09-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000012||Oreif||02-09-2001||12:34 AM||||William, The reason it "Thumps" is because the bass blockers cut out the frequencies the speakers cannot reproduce so now they will push the mid range bass harder (no distortion). The reason they sound like they have bass is due to how close you sit to the speakers. Sort of like headphones. Very tiny speakers but they can get the bass freq's out of them.<BR>I think the seat speakers are very good for imaging in the car. Especially since the driver and the passenger get their own set.<BR>I have heard stock and aftermarket speakers in the seats and in my opinion both sets sounded good. I wish I knew why they stopped them after the 1985 model year.<p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 02-09-2001).]||||reg||14
Z||000013||TwisT||02-09-2001||06:26 PM||||Can anyone recommend what size/ brand will work?  I'm very interested now that you guys have said how great they sound.<P>Brett||||reg||1
