Z||000016||Oreif||02-09-2001||09:09 PM||||Polk Audio, Kenwood, Infinity, MB Quart, Pioneer, Sony, Alpine, JVC, Clarion, and JBL<BR>All make 3 1/2" speakers. Just go to a Best Buy and listen to them.||||reg||1
Z||000017||Homicidal||02-09-2001||09:42 PM||||Look at it this way:<P>Headrest speakers = Left + Right on each seat = 6 Speakers system.<P>Sail Panels = One set left and right speakers, 4 speakers system.<P>Headrest speakers rule!||||reg||1
Z||000018||Oreif||02-10-2001||09:47 AM||||4 Woofers<BR>+<BR>4 tweeters<BR>+<BR>1 Subwoofer<BR>=<BR>9 Speaker System!<BR>(my sail panels have 2 speakers each!)<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><BR>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 02-10-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000019||286SE'S||02-12-2001||03:33 PM||||No need to change the 3 1/2" speaker to 4" since ou do not need more bass. An aftermarket speaker would have a separate tweeter and give a better high end.<BR>OREIF:<BR>9 speakers..So that is the factory setup for<BR>performance sound, right? I noticed all the performace sound speakers have separate tweeters and the others don't.||||reg||1
Z||000020||Gold-86SE||02-12-2001||04:22 PM||||<BR>It is my understanding that the headrest speaker seats were discontinued due to high theft claims during 84 and 85.  Theives obviously knew a great product when they saw it.<P>------------------<BR>84 SE 4.10 4 Speed (Cold and Rain Daily Driver)<BR>85 GT Automatic (Restoration Project)<BR>86 SE 4 Speed (Fair Weather Daily Driver)<BR>87 SC 5 Speed (Not Running, V8 Conversion?)<BR>Please visit my <A HREF="http://www.trifocus.net/~fws/index.html" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Work Shop</A>||||reg||1
