Z||000022||overlord||02-13-2001||11:28 PM||||i really wanna upgrade my seat speakers to something better.....i kinda looked at takin off the seat cover last year and that kind of turned me away from the subject  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">.<P>Think ill give er another go||||reg||1
Z||000023||sqoach||02-14-2001||12:02 AM||||hey now, no trash talkin' of the sail panel speakers. mine happen to sound real good, even though they're just 2-way jensen's. plus i have another set of surface mount speakers back there. they're 3-way seperates in a way. got a 5 1/4 woofer, 1 1/2 mid, and a 3/4 tweeter. plus the 4x10s and i'm getting some 5 1/4 or 6 1/2 for the doors, and then a 10" sub for some serious bass. i guess that's a 13 speaker system if you count those surface mount ones as 3 since they're seperate.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>sqoach@yahoo.com<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mysig2.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000024||Oreif||02-14-2001||12:26 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 286SE'S:<BR><B>No need to change the 3 1/2" speaker to 4" since ou do not need more bass. An aftermarket speaker would have a separate tweeter and give a better high end.<BR>OREIF:<BR>9 speakers..So that is the factory setup for<BR>performance sound, right? I noticed all the performace sound speakers have separate tweeters and the others don't.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>No, the factory set-up for performance was 5 speakers. (2 front 2 rear and one sub) I have upgraded mine to sound a whole lot better than that.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000025||Philphine||02-14-2001||11:56 AM||||i've only since last spring had a fiero with the headrest speakers but i like them. i keep them turned down so low that i don't think i'll ever have to worry about blowing them and if i put a system in one of my 84's i'll probaly add xovers to protect them more.<P>one thing i'm wondering. i may get some decent aftermarket seat covers that are some kind of vinyl (saw them in pepboys. look good for universal covers). since they wont have the speaker holes i'm wondering how much or how badly the sound will be muffled.  ||||reg||1
Z||000026||Neverfinished||02-14-2001||12:05 PM||||I have sheep skin seat cover and they don't muffle them that much. They don't sound any different with regular seat covers. I had k-mart covers on before and they are too thin to block the speakers||||reg||1
